   "source": [
    "# Finding static locations with Gradient Descent (Baseline Approach) \n",
    "\n",
    "Credits: JonathanWhitaker\n",
    "\n",
    "To do the gradient descent we'll rely on PyTorch to calculate gradients. If you're not familiar with tensors and this part looks scary, check out the fastai lossons that cover SGD from scratch (Lessons 3 and 4 of the new course and this book chapter:https://github.com/fastai/fastbook/blob/master/04_mnist_basics.ipynb). This is where I got a lot of the inspiration for this code.\n",
    "\n",
    "I start with 6 random locations that are close to the center of the crashes - plot these over the crashes and see if this initialization seems sensible."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 42,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Q_Nc0rwFyzdh",
    "outputId": "f0f0ac08-3dc9-410b-96c1-53e66d524c07"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "tensor([[-1.3068, 36.8233],\n",
       "        [-1.2683, 36.8502],\n",
       "        [-1.2853, 36.8710],\n",
       "        [-1.2811, 36.8656],\n",
       "        [-1.2716, 36.8456],\n",
       "        [-1.2775, 36.8582]], requires_grad=True)"
      ]
